 "overview": {
  "summary": "The instrument's resistance standard. A10 holds every fixed resistance value the calibrator can output from 10 Ω to 100 MΩ -- everything except the 1 Ω, 1.9 Ω and short, which live on the Ohms Cal assembly (A9). It is an almost entirely passive board: three Fluke hermetically sealed thin-film resistor networks (Z1, Z2, Z3), one discrete 90 MΩ film resistor (R1), 39 relays, nine relay driver ICs, two decoders and exactly one op amp. The values are arranged as two ladders sharing a common low end -- a 1x10ⁿ decade string and a 1.9x10ⁿ string. Z2 carries the 1x high decades (9 M, 900 k, 90 k, 9 k), Z3 the 1.9x high decades (17.1 M, 1.71 M, 171 k, 17.1 k), and Z1 carries the low decades of BOTH strings in one package (900, 90, 10 for the 1x side and 1710, 171, 19 for the 1.9x side), which is why it is drawn twice on sheet 1. The 100 MΩ value is R1's 90 MΩ inserted in series with the decade string above its 10 MΩ tap, and it is the only two-wire value on the board. Relays K1 and K2 (reset) connect the top of the selected string to INT OUT HI and INT SENSE HI; K27A/B and K39A/B connect the two strings' low ends to OHMS OUT LO and OHMS SENSE LO. A10 has no processor and no diagnostic multiplexer: every relay on it is driven from the 82C55 on A9 across the motherboard, and every self-test reading of it is taken by the adc on the DAC assembly (A11) through A9's differential amplifier. U1, an OPA111, is used only during calibration -- it is a low-bias-current buffer for values above 1 MΩ. K3, K28 and K31-K34 are calibration-only relays; K4 and K6 belong to A9's two-wire compensation circuit.",
  "connectors": "P301 and P302, both DIN 41612 type C, 64-pin right-angle, into the Analog Motherboard (A3), where they are called J301 and J302. P301 carries the analog signals: INT OUT HI (30A/30C), INT SENSE HI (28A/28C), OHMS SENSE LO (25A/25C), OHMS OUT LO (24A/24C), OHMS SENSE HI (22A/22C), OHMS OUT HI (21A/21C), 10V OUT HI (1A/1C), 10V SENSE HI (2A), 10V SENSE LO (23A/23C), DAC OUT LO (11A/11C), ACOM (2C), AMP IN (3C) and AMP OUT (3A). P302 carries the supplies and the digital control: +17 S (30A/30C), S COM (32A/32C), -17 S (31A/31C), +5 RLH (23A/23C) with RLH COM (25A/25C), +5 LH (22A/22C) with LH COM (24A/24C), and the 82C55 lines from A9 as OHM PA0-PA7, OHM PB0-PB3, OHM PC0-PC3 and OHM PC4. Every analog pair is wired A and C in parallel.",
  "source": "§2-168 … §2-172; Figure 7-10 sheets 1 and 2 (connector pin fields read off the sheets)"
 },
