    "note": "The only analog supply on the board, and it feeds exactly one device: U1, an OPA111 in a TO-99 can, inside a dashed region on sheet 1 annotated GROUND PLANE = SCOM. +17 S reaches U1 pin 7 through VR1, a 3.3 V zener in series, so the positive supply node sits about 3.3 V below the rail; -17 S reaches pin 4 through R5 (100 Ω), which at the OPA111's few milliamps drops almost nothing. C3 (10 µF tantalum) and C1 (0.22 µF polyester) bypass the positive node to SCOM, C4 and C2 the negative one. R3 (270 Ω) is the feedback element from pin 6 to pin 2 and R2 (270 Ω) sits in the +17 S feed to the input network. Nothing else on A10 runs on these rails -- if U1 is not the suspect, ±17 S is not either. A10 makes no supply of its own and has no regulator.",
